---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { agents } from "../data/agents.js";
import { features, workflows } from "../data/topics.js";
import { siteBase } from "../utils/site.js";
---
<BaseLayout title="Agent Decision Kit — Fast Local Browser Tools for Coding Agents" description="An open-source local-first MCP server and CLI for Playwright browser automation, typed decisions, context pruning, model routing, and code-agent workflows." canonicalPath="">
  <main>
    <section class="hero shell">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> OPEN SOURCE · LOCAL FIRST · EXPERIMENTAL ALPHA</p>
        <h1>Give coding agents<br />a <span>faster next step.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Small, bounded decisions and browser actions for the agent loops that do real work. A local MCP server. A short list of controls. A clear approval boundary.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="primary" href={`${siteBase}features/browser-agent/`}>Explore browser tools <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit">View the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="trust"><span>Apache-2.0</span><i></i><span>Node.js 20.19+</span><i></i><span>No product telemetry</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="window-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><code>localhost · browser-demo.html</code></div>
        <img class="demo-shot" src={`${siteBase}images/demo-browser.png`} alt="Playwright screenshot of the local fake-data browser demo page" width="1100" height="700" />
        <div class="overlay"><span class="check">✓</span><div><b>Resettable demo</b><small>Fake tasks · no account or customer data</small></div><span class="duration">DEMO</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE DECISION LOOP</p><h2>Keep perception and execution<br /><span>simple. Make the choice explicit.</span></h2><p>Inspect a bounded state, select a typed option, validate it, and let ordinary code handle the action.</p></div>
      <img class="flow" src={`${siteBase}images/decision-flow.svg`} alt="Browser flow: inspect visible controls, choose a bounded action, approve only when sensitive, then execute and return a delta" width="1000" height="250" loading="lazy" />
      <img class="architecture" src={`${siteBase}images/architecture.svg`} alt="Architecture diagram showing the coding agent, local tools, decision provider, separate user approval gate, result validation, and deterministic execution" width="1200" height="500" loading="lazy" />
    </section>

    <section class="section alt">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND BROWSER USE</p><h2>Fast path is the page<br /><span>the browser already knows.</span></h2><p>Read accessible DOM controls before reaching for a screenshot. Keep candidate labels bounded, form values out of the snapshot, and sensitive clicks behind a second call.</p></div>
        <div class="browser-grid">
          <div class="browser-copy">
            <div class="mini-step"><span>01</span><div><b>Inspect visible controls</b><p>Get buttons, links, supported text/date fields, and native select options.</p></div></div>
            <div class="mini-step"><span>02</span><div><b>Choose or select a ref</b><p>Use the local model, or tell the agent exactly which control to click.</p></div></div>
            <div class="mini-step"><span>03</span><div><b>Review the page change</b><p>Return the changed excerpt. Ask the user before consequential actions.</p></div></div>
            <a class="text-link" href={`${siteBase}features/browser-agent/`}>How browser actions work <span>→</span></a>
          </div>
          <img src={`${siteBase}images/browser-demo.gif`} alt="Short recording of a local Playwright browser interacting with the safe demo page" width="800" height="520" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">COMPOSABLE BUILDING BLOCKS</p><h2>Small tools for the<br /><span>steps between big prompts.</span></h2></div>
      <div class="cards">
        {features.map((feature) => <a class="card" href={`${siteBase}${feature.canonicalPath}`}><span class="card-icon">↗</span><h3>{feature.short}</h3><p>{feature.description}</p><span class="card-link">Read the guide →</span></a>)}
        {workflows.slice(0,3).map((workflow) => <a class="card" href={`${siteBase}${workflow.canonicalPath}`}><span class="card-icon">⌘</span><h3>{workflow.short}</h3><p>{workflow.description}</p><span class="card-link">Read the guide →</span></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section metrics alt">
      <div class="shell metric-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">SMALL, REPRODUCIBLE SMOKE RUNS</p><h2>Measure first.<br /><span>Claim only what we can show.</span></h2><p>The latest 26-task multi-tool MiniWoB integration completed 23/26 with no harness timeouts, on the same task set, seed, and action cap as the preceding run. Pointer-target deduplication restored the nested menu task while the exact-sender email task stayed successful. Ten native checkboxes are set in one <code>browser_set_checkboxes</code> call; <code>browser_copy_field</code> copies generated text locally, and <code>browser_set_range</code> handles keyboard-operated sliders. Each submit still uses a separate local-only synthetic approval. This is bounded tool integration, not an autonomous-agent score. On Linux CPU, end-to-end latency including reset was p50 1.192 s / p95 23.342 s; browser action-loop p50 was 361 ms / p95 22.317 s; four measured decision calls had p95 692 ms. The long tail includes two visual-only task descriptions that took tens of seconds and still failed. The remaining misses are <code>ascending-numbers</code>, <code>daily-calendar</code>, and <code>read-table-2</code>. A separate focused eight-task run passed 8/8 with browser-loop p50 305 ms / p95 699 ms. These CPU samples are not general speed guarantees, and decision estimates remain uncalibrated. A separate 30-case decision fixture scored 7/10 Choice and 5/10 yes/no, with 1.04 Score MAE on a 0–4 scale; its examples are not held out.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${siteBase}benchmarks/`}>Read the benchmark results →</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/README.md">Read the protocol and raw runs →</a></div><div class="metric-card metric-stack"><div class="metric-stat"><div class="metric-number">23/26</div><div><b>Latest multi-tool integration</b><small>26 curated tasks · Linux CPU · no timeouts</small></div></div><div class="metric-stat"><div class="metric-number">8/8</div><div><b>Focused browser smoke</b><small>8 curated tasks · separate Linux CPU run</small></div></div></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell agents-section">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">STANDARD MCP · LOCAL STDIO</p><h2>Your coding agent.<br /><span>One consistent tool set.</span></h2><p>Use the config guide for your client. Setup snippets show local source paths until the npm package is released.</p></div>
      <div class="agent-list">{agents.map((agent) => <a href={`${siteBase}${agent.canonicalPath}`}><span>{agent.number}</span><b>{agent.name}</b><small>{agent.family}</small><i>↗</i></a>)}</div>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${siteBase}agents/`}>Browse all client setup guides →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta shell">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">TRY IT ON A PAGE YOU CAN RESET</p><h2>Start with the local demo.</h2><p>Use fake data, inspect the visible actions, and see how a small browser choice returns a small result.</p></div>
      <a class="primary" href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/examples/browser-demo.html">Open the demo source ↗</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .shell{max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:28px;padding-right:28px}.hero{position:relative;min-height:600px;padding-top:83px;padding-bottom:54px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.92fr 1.08fr;gap:44px;align-items:center;overflow:hidden}.hero-copy{position:relative;z-index:2}.eyebrow{color:var(--mint);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;font-weight:800;font-size:11px}.pulse{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;background:var(--mint);border-radius:50%;margin-right:9px;box-shadow:0 0 0 5px #75e2c21a}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(46px,6vw,76px);line-height:.99;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:22px 0}.hero h1 span,.section-heading h2 span{color:var(--mint)}.lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:18px;line-height:1.65;max-width:490px}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:26px}.primary,.secondary{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;border-radius:11px;padding:13px 17px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px}.primary{background:var(--mint);color:#07121a;box-shadow:0 8px 30px #75e2c225}.primary:hover{color:#07121a;background:#a1f5dc}.secondary{color:#e0edf8;border:1px solid #34526d}.trust{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-top:27px;font-size:12px;color:#91a5b9}.trust i{width:3px;height:3px;border-radius:50%;background:#48637d}.hero-visual{position:relative;z-index:2;background:#0d1b2b;border:1px solid #324b61;padding:10px;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:0 25px 85px #0008;transform:rotate(.5deg)}.window-bar{height:32px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:0 7px}.window-bar>span{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:#4d6478}.window-bar>span:first-child{background:#f1857f}.window-bar>span:nth-child(2){background:#e6c46a}.window-bar>span:nth-child(3){background:#70ce9c}.window-bar code{margin-left:auto;color:#87a0b8;font-size:10px}.demo-shot{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #213b51}.overlay{position:absolute;bottom:24px;left:22px;right:22px;padding:13px 15px;background:#0b1c2beF;border:1px solid #466a7d;border-radius:12px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;box-shadow:0 10px 30px #0006}.check{width:25px;height:25px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#164438;color:#9df2d5}.overlay div{display:grid;gap:3px}.overlay b{font-size:12px}.overlay small{font-size:10px;color:#9cb0c4}.duration{margin-left:auto;color:var(--mint);font:700 10px ui-monospace,monospace}.hero-glow{position:absolute;top:70px;right:100px;width:410px;height:410px;background:#286d7b26;filter:blur(90px);border-radius:50%}.section{padding-top:86px;padding-bottom:32px}.section-heading{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 34px;text-align:center}.section-heading h2,.metric-inner h2{font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,55px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.052em;margin:14px 0}.section-heading>p:last-child,.metric-inner>div>p:not(.eyebrow){color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;font-size:16px}.flow,.architecture{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.architecture{margin-top:12px}.alt{margin-top:38px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#0c1928,#0b1725);border-top:1px solid #ffffff0c;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff0c}.alt>.shell,.alt .shell{padding-top:75px;padding-bottom:72px}.browser-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.68fr 1.32fr;gap:36px;align-items:center}.browser-copy{display:grid;gap:24px}.mini-step{display:flex;gap:14px}.mini-step>span{font:700 12px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--mint);padding-top:3px}.mini-step b{font-size:15px}.mini-step p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;margin:6px 0 0}.browser-grid img{width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #2d465d;border-radius:16px;box-shadow:0 20px 70px #0006}.text-link{display:inline-flex;gap:10px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;font-size:14px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px}.card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:225px;padding:23px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:15px;text-decoration:none;transition:transform .18s ease,border-color .18s ease}.card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);border-color:#5ab99e}.card-icon{width:34px;height:34px;display:grid;place-items:center;border:1px solid #34526d;border-radius:10px;color:var(--mint)}.card h3{margin:17px 0 8px;color:var(--text);font-size:17px}.card p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 18px}.card-link{margin-top:auto;font-size:12px;color:var(--mint)}.metric-inner{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 320px;align-items:center;gap:70px}.metric-inner>div>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:620px}.metric-card{position:relative;min-height:245px;background:#0b1827;border:1px solid #2b4156;border-radius:18px;padding:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:10px;overflow:hidden}.metric-number{font-size:72px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.07em;color:var(--mint)}.metric-card b{font-size:15px}.metric-card small{max-width:240px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55}.agents-section .section-heading{margin-bottom:26px}.agent-list{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:22px}.agent-list a{display:grid;grid-template-columns:42px 1fr 150px 22px;align-items:center;gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:15px 6px;text-decoration:none}.agent-list a>span{color:var(--mint);font:700 11px ui-monospace,monospace}.agent-list b{color:var(--text);font-size:14px}.agent-list small{color:#91a5b9;font-size:12px}.agent-list i{font-style:normal}.cta{margin-top:95px;margin-bottom:40px;padding-top:35px;padding-bottom:35px;border:1px solid #2a4559;background:linear-gradient(112deg,#102739,#0d1b2b);border-radius:20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:30px}.cta h2{font-size:30px;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:9px 0}.cta p:not(.eyebrow){color:var(--muted);max-width:560px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6}.cta .primary{white-space:nowrap}
  @media(max-width:900px){.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:32px;padding-top:62px}.hero-copy{max-width:700px}.hero-visual{max-width:760px}.browser-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.browser-copy{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.browser-copy .text-link{grid-column:1/-1}.metric-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr 260px;gap:28px}.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.shell{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}.hero{padding-top:48px;min-height:auto}.hero h1{font-size:48px}.lead{font-size:16px}.trust{flex-wrap:wrap}.section{padding-top:65px}.section-heading{text-align:left}.browser-copy{grid-template-columns:1fr}.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.metric-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr}.metric-card{min-height:200px}.agent-list a{grid-template-columns:32px 1fr 20px}.agent-list small{display:none}.agent-list i{grid-column:3;grid-row:1}.cta{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column;margin-top:65px}.overlay{left:14px;right:14px;bottom:16px}.overlay small{max-width:180px}}
  .metric-stack{display:grid;gap:16px}.metric-stat{display:grid;grid-template-columns:110px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;align-items:center}.metric-stat .metric-number{font-size:48px;white-space:nowrap}.metric-stat small{display:block;margin-top:5px;font-size:11px;max-width:none}.metric-stack{min-height:245px}
  @media(max-width:900px){.metric-stat{grid-template-columns:88px minmax(0,1fr);gap:8px}.metric-stat .metric-number{font-size:38px}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.metric-stat{grid-template-columns:100px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px}.metric-stat .metric-number{font-size:46px}}
</style>
